{{Quote|Nothing's free on Nal Hutta.|An [[Ithorian]] [[bartender]], to Anakin Skywalker|<ref name="Friends and Enemies" />}}
'''Nal Hutta''', also known simply as '''Hutta''', was a [[Temperature|hot]], [[swamp]]y [[planet]] located deep within [[Hutt Space]] of [[the galaxy]] that was the [[homeworld]] of the [[Hutt]] [[species]] and [[Capital|headquarters]] of the [[Grand Hutt Council]]. Nal Hutta was a major haven for both the government&mdash;aligned [[Hutt Clan]] and other criminal elements of the [[galaxy]], located far from galactic authorities. Its terrain was largely bloated swamps and bogs coated in greasy rains, all of which were greatly exacerbated by the [[Drengir crisis]] during the [[High Republic Era]].

==Description==
{{Quote|On this slime pool, everybody's an outlaw.|[[Cad Bane]], on Nal Hutta|<ref name="Friends and Enemies" />}}
Nal Hutta, known also as just Hutta<ref name="Tribes of Tatooine">{{BOBF|Chapter 2: The Tribes of Tatooine}}</ref> was a ringed [[planet]] nestled in the depths of [[Hutt Space]]<ref name="BtMF">{{BuildFalconCite|81|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref> and was located in the [[Outer Rim Territories]]<ref name="The Visual Dictionary" /> and [[The Slice]]. <ref name="Explorer's Guide" /> It was a mist-covered [[swamp]] world<ref name="BtMF" /> with a [[Temperature|hot]], humid<ref name="VE" /> and fetid [[Atmosphere|climate]] maintained by thick swampy [[Water|rain]] that fell almost perpetually.<ref name="BtMF" /> The world was a hotbed of life<ref name="VE" /> and its environment was fairly representative of the [[Sentience|sentient]] [[Hutt]] [[species]] that inhabited the world.<ref name="BtMF" /> The influence of the Hutts made the world an important location.<ref name="VE" /> The planet's surface was covered with numerous bogs<ref name="Nal Hutta" /> with what little solid land there was claimed by the Hutts and used to support their homes.<ref name="BtMF" />

The Hutts built only a handful of [[spaceport]]s on the surface of Nal Hutta in order to connect their towns, settlements, and palaces, as the planet received few visitors due to most business with offworlders being conducted on the planet's largest [[moon]], [[Nar Shaddaa]]. The foremost of these spaceports was the planet's [[capital]] [[city]], [[Bilbousa]], a sprawling mess covered in arching roots that spread out from looming bulbous pods. Within sight of the city was the [[Gardulla the Hutt's Palace|Palace]] of [[Gardulla Besadii the Elder]], one of the largest buildings on Nal Hutta, which served as the occasional headquarters of the [[Grand Hutt Council]], the ruling body that both worked and led the [[Hutt Clan]]. Under the Hutt's control, the planet shared a reputation with Nar Shaddaa for being polluted and dangerous, but played a leading role in the galaxy's shadow economy.<ref name="BtMF" />

==History==
===Transformed into a swamp===
The Hutt Clan was based off Nal Hutta.<ref name="Hunt for Ziro" /> Once, Nal Hutta was a planet full of teeming cities. The world was [[Attack on Nal Hutta|changed]] during the [[Drengir crisis]], with a [[Drengir]] infestation drastically expanding reach of the planet's [[jungle]]s,<ref name="Rising Storm">''[[The High Republic: The Rising Storm]]''</ref> a climatic shift with effects that would remain for [[Standard year|years]] to come.<ref name="Hunt for Ziro" /> Luckily, the new environment<ref name="Rising Storm" /> was one the Hutts were already particularly well-suited for.<ref name="Nal Hutta" />

===Clone Wars===
After [[Senate hostage crisis|freeing]] [[Ziro Desilijic Tiure|Ziro]] the Hutt from [[Republic Judiciary Central Detention Center|prison]] on [[Coruscant]], the [[bounty hunter]] [[Cad Bane]] brought the fugitive Hutt to the Grand Hutt Council on Nal Hutta. Ziro refused to divulge the location of his secret [[holodiary]] and was [[Prison|imprisoned]] by the Hutt Council. However, Ziro managed to escape with the help of the singer [[Sy Snootles]]. The [[Jedi Master]]s [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and [[Quinlan Vos]] traveled to Nal Hutta to apprehend Ziro. However, Ziro and Snootles escaped offworld with the help of Ziro's [[Mama]].<ref name="Hunt for Ziro" />

While on an undercover mission to save [[Supreme Chancellor]] [[Darth Sidious|Palpatine]] from [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist]] [[assassin]]s, Kenobi, who was disguised as the [[bounty]] hunter [[Rako Hardeen]], and the fugitives Bane and [[Moralo Eval]] crash-landed on the swamps of Nal Hutta. The trio traveled to [[Bilbousa Bazaar]] where they obtained a [[starship]] to travel offworld. Despite being pursued by the [[Jedi Knight]] [[Anakin Skywalker]] and [[Padawan]] [[Ahsoka Tano]], "Hardeen" and the bounty hunters managed to escape offworld to [[Orondia]].<ref name="Friends and Enemies" />

During the later stage of the [[Clone Wars]], the former [[Sith apprentice]] [[Maul]], his brother [[Savage Opress]], and the [[Shadow Collective]] [[Mission to Nal Hutta|visited]] Nal Hutta in an attempt to force the Hutt Council to join their [[Shadow Collective]]. The Hutts rejected their demands and a gun battle broke out between the Shadow Collective and various bounty hunters hired by the Hutts. The Hutt Council escaped but Maul's party managed to capture [[Oruba]], who revealed that [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure]] was on [[Tatooine]]. After [[Death|killing]] Oruba, the Shadow Collective [[Attack on Jabba's Palace|departed]] for Tatooine.<ref name="Eminence">{{TCW|Eminence (episode)}}</ref>

===Imperial era===
During the [[Imperial Era]], between the [[Standard year|years]] [[3 ABY|3]] and [[4 ABY]],<ref name="BH 24 Date">The events of [[Bounty Hunters 24|''Bounty Hunters'' 24]] take place after the [[Escape from Cloud City]] and before the [[Rescue of Han Solo]], which are dated to [[3 ABY]] and [[4 ABY]], respectively, by ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''.</ref> the [[Crimson Dawn]] [[flagship]] [[Vermillion (Crimson Dawn)|''Vermillion'']] traveled to Nal Hutta and landed in the [[Bilbousa Spaceport]]. Meanwhile, the bounty hunter [[T'onga]] and her [[T'onga's crew|crew]] also arrived in Bilbousa to [[Raid on the Vermillion|raid]] the ''Vermillion'' and rescue the [[Youngling|child]] [[Cadeliah]] who had been taken [[prisoner]] and was behind held on the flagship.<ref name="Bounty Hunters 24">[[Bounty Hunters 24|''Bounty Hunters'' 24]]</ref>

===New Republic era===
A pair of Hutt siblings known as [[The Twins]] were based on Nal Hutta<ref name="Tribes of Tatooine" /> by [[9 ABY]].<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> [[Daimyo]] [[Boba Fett]], with whom the Twins would go on to compete with for control of [[Jabba's criminal empire]] on Tatooine, considered their lifestyle on Hutta to be debaucherous.<ref name="Tribes of Tatooine" /> By [[28 ABY]], Nal Hutta was still considered a crime haven by many within the [[New Republic]].<ref name="Bloodline">[[Bloodline (novel)|''Bloodline'']]</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|George Lucas had some very specific ideas about Nal Hutta. He gave us some really rough sketches. There was to be this very swampy, these big pustual orbs sticking up where they would build their palaces.|Dave Filoni|<ref name="Hutts and the Underworld">{{HomeVideoCite|set=Star Wars: The Clone Wars The Complete Season Three|featurette=Hutts and the Underworld}}</ref>}}
Nal Hutta was first depicted in the episode ''[[Hunt for Ziro]]'' of ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'', based on George Lucas' ideas and sketches of how he envisioned the world.<ref name="Hutts and the Underworld" />

